# The public binary drop (docs/releases.md, "The public binary drop"): the compiled proprietary
# parts of one engine pin, so a source build outside the org can link them instead of compiling
# private sources it does not have. Built by scripts/make-binary-drop.sh; published by hand.
#
# A build takes the drop with -DONEBIT_BINARY_DROP=<path or URL>. A URL is only accepted when this
# file pins its sha256 for the engine commit being built; a mismatch stops the configure. A path is
# verified against the drop's own MANIFEST (every file's sha256) and must have been built from the
# same engine commit.
#
# url_pattern: the release asset's location. %(version)s and %(engine_sha)s are substituted.
# drop=: one line per published drop: drop=<engine_sha> <version> <sha256 of the .tar.zst>
#
# Moving this file is part of publishing a drop: add its line, or builds from a URL for that pin
# are refused. Nothing here is fetched at build time unless ONEBIT_BINARY_DROP names a URL.
url_pattern=https://github.com/1bit-MONSTER/engine/releases/download/binary-drop-%(version)s/binary-drop-%(version)s-linux-x86_64.tar.zst

# No drop is published yet: the first line appears when the orchestrator publishes one.
# drop=<40-char engine sha> <version> <64-char sha256>
